{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q134192","formula":"C₄H₁₀","hill":"C4H10","elements":["H","C"],"composition":{"C":4.0,"H":10.0},"names":{"en":"Butane","ru":"Бутан","uk":"Бутан"},"descriptions":{"en":"Butane () is an alkane with the formula C4H10. Butane exists as two isomers, n-butane, CH3CH2CH2CH3 and iso-butane, (CH3)3CH. Both isomers are highly flammable, colorless, easily liquefied gases that quickly vaporize at room temperature and pressure. Butanes are a trace component of natural gases, which contain higher concentrations of other hydrocarbons such as propane, ethane, and especially methane.","ru":"Бута́н (C4H10) — органическое соединение, углеводород класса алканов. В химии название используется в основном для обозначения н-бутана. Такое же название имеет смесь н-бутана и его изомера изобутана CH(CH3)3.","uk":"Бута́н (англ. Butane, нім. Butan) — насичена вуглеводнева органічна сполука із молекулярною формулою С4H10 (CH3CH2CH2CH3), газ без кольору й запаху."},"fame":77,"pubchemCid":7843,"mass":58.12,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCC","inchikey":"IJDNQMDRQITEOD-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"butane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"7843","atoms":14,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.563,"y":0.516,"z":0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":0.563,"y":-0.516,"z":0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.929,"y":-0.151,"z":-0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":1.929,"y":0.15,"z":-0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.472,"y":1.167,"z":-0.871,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.482,"y":1.155,"z":0.894,"el":"H"},{"x":0.482,"y":-1.155,"z":0.894,"el":"H"},{"x":0.472,"y":-1.167,"z":-0.871,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.054,"y":-0.771,"z":-0.9,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.065,"y":-0.786,"z":0.874,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.72,"y":0.606,"z":-0.006,"el":"H"},{"x":2.054,"y":0.771,"z":-0.9,"el":"H"},{"x":2.72,"y":-0.606,"z":-0.006,"el":"H"},{"x":2.065,"y":0.785,"z":0.874,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[